  "notes": "{正|せい} is used as a prefix or noun meaning \"positive\" (math) or \"correct/official.\"\n\nMATH USAGE:\n- {正|せい}の{数|すう}: positive number\n- {正|せい}の{符号|ふごう}: plus sign (+)\n- Opposite: {負|ふ} (negative)\n- {正|せい}{三角形|さんかくけい}: equilateral triangle\n\nMEANING \"CORRECT/OFFICIAL\":\n- {正|せい}{解|かい}: correct answer\n- {正|せい}{式|しき}: official, formal\n- {正|せい}{社員|しゃいん}: regular (full-time) employee\n- {正|せい}{門|もん}: main gate\n\nCONFUSION ALERT:\n- {正|せい}: positive, correct\n- {製|せい}: made in/of ({日本|にほん}{製|せい} = made in Japan)\n- {性|せい}: nature, gender, -ness\n\nThese homophones are common sources of confusion.",
